README -> for setting up batch SQP runs and conducting sensitivity analysis

For setting up batch SQP runs:
1) Open agrivoltaics_multistart_SQP.m
2) Set N_lhs value (line 12)->initial num of design points you want excluding the default DV point
3) Ensure you have Matlab Parallel Toolbox installed -> otherwise change the parfor loop to a for loop
4) Run agrivoltaics_multistart_SQP.m --> for reference, 72 runs took about 1.5 hours to run in parallel on my M3 Macbook pro, where I had 8 parallel 'workers'
5) Once agrivoltaics_multistart_SQP.m is done, it will have returned (1) a timestamped multistart_SQP_results CSV file (2) a summary printed to command window of all SQP runs, (3) saved x_star.mat file with best DVs found and obj. value (4) a breakdown of x_star results, printed to command window (5) specific per-iteration convergence info for best run saved to conv_history.mat + a convergence plot

For running and plotting sensitivity analysis:
1) open and run run_sensitivity.m (also uses Matlab parallel Toolbox)
2) open plot_sensitvity.m 
3) change the file names in lines 10 and 11 to the relevant .mat files from run_sensitvity.m (e.g. dv_sensitivity_20260324_172911.mat)
4) run plot_sensitvity.m

alternatively...
1) Run plot_sensitvity.m  on its own to see plots used in A3b Q3
